{"claims":[{"claim_text":"This resolution builds on the electoral standards of the Anti-Zionist Resolution introduced by Ahmed H. and passed by the 2023-2025 National Political Committee and over 56 DSA chapters, continuing to provide a material counterweight to the Zionist lobby.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"This resolution expands uptake of the Stop Fueling Genocide, No Appetite for Apartheid, and Mask Off Maersk campaigns.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"This resolution establishes an Arms Embargo Steering Committee to increase coordination across labor, legislative, and community organizing efforts to disrupt the flow of weapons to Israel.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"This resolution supports chapters in pursuing divestment through pressure campaigns and ballot initiatives.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"This resolution develops strategies to protect the movement and build resilience against state repression.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"This resolution prioritizes a grassroots approach to resisting fascism and presents three strategic points of activation where DSA can make an incisive intervention: making immigrant defense an organizational priority through a national Abolish ICE campaign, supporting chapters in building local and state-level campaigns around abolitionist demands, and scaling up the ability to fight state repression by strengthening Red Rabbits and building infrastructure to support comrades facing repression.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[2]},{"claim_text":"Two important political events in 2028 – the presidential elections and the labor movement’s response to the UAW call for a May Day strike – present crucial opportunities for agitational mass organizing.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[4]},{"claim_text":"This resolution makes it a priority for DSA to take incremental steps to explore building a broad Left-Labor electoral coalition capable of organizing the foundation of independence from the duopoly.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[4]},{"claim_text":"This resolution directs DSA to convene a 2028 Planning Committee to explore the viability of different organizing strategies, liaise across national bodies, and build local chapter preparedness in preparation for 2028.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[4]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
